            "name": "5. Security Tests",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "IP Whitelist — How it works",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "X-API-KEY",
                                "value": "{{api_key}}"
                            },
                            {
                                "key": "X-API-SECRET",
                                "value": "{{api_secret}}"
                            }
                        ],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/partner/balance",
                            "host": [
                                "{{base_url}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "partner",
                                "balance"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "**IP Whitelist Behavior:**\n\n- If `allowed_ips` is **empty** → ALL IPs are allowed (open mode, useful for development)\n- If `allowed_ips` has entries → ONLY those IPs are allowed; all others get 403\n\nThis is why 127.0.0.1 works even without explicit whitelisting — the list is empty.\n\nTo restrict access: add specific IPs in the Vendor Developer > IP Whitelist section."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Correct Key + Wrong Secret (expect 401)",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "X-API-KEY",
                                "value": "{{api_key}}"
                            },
                            {
